A timer written at the root of a file.

The package body is a view body like a window's, so a statement in it that is
not a window is lowered and emitted where it stands. It was not: passRootWindow
took the windows out of that body and cleared what was left, so a
`time.timer(…)` at the root of a file -- or in a root component's body, the
other body it cleared -- reached no backend at all and said nothing about it.
Every other timer fixture in this repository puts one inside a window, which is
why nothing caught it. Deleting the pass is the whole of the fix; there was
nothing to add.

Three targets, because a timer has more than one answer and the gap was in
front of all of them: bubbletea keeps the primitive and reads the schedule off
the node, while fyne and html override `timer` with an `effect` over a host
start/stop pair.

deny out/go/bubbletea/model.go `func \(m Model\) Init\(\) tea.Cmd \{\n\treturn nil` -- the tick is scheduled from Init; an Init that returns nil is the dropped timer this fixture is for
deny out/none/html/index.html `var state = \{\s*\}` -- the tick writes `ticks`, so the page declares it

-- app.sngl --
import time "sngl:time"
import ui "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
    }
    none {
        html
    }
}

var ticks = 0

time.timer(interval=1000ms, @tick {
    ticks = ticks + 1
})

ui.window #w(title="t") {
    ui.text(value="{ticks}")
}
